Native QuickJS core

    mk install

Builds /$objtype/lib/libquickjs.a with the Plan 9 compiler and native libc.
The source and math routines are shared with the APE build; see ../UPSTREAM.
Native libc support is in ../native.h and native.c. No std/os event
loop or POSIX I/O layer is included. The first client is ../../rayjs.

Compile clients with -p -DPLAN9 -DPLAN9_NATIVE -D_$objtype and include
../quickjs.h, which supplies the native headers. Link libquickjs.a before
other libraries so its IEEE 754 math implementations are selected.
For tests, run mk test in ../../rayjs (native) and .. (APE).
